rota lap 4553, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes: I ran the capacity instrument up close instead of reading the sentence about it, and the reading disagreed with the story five ships were telling.
think Opened with fleet_round_open.sh, which fetched, found the anointed order already held, and reported five dead-letter files. Cold roster pass detached to session-output/standing-equipment-cold.txt; held still while it ran.
think Reds first. The cold pass read six red. Two were mine to close and one link long -- fold_shelf_link and fold_shelf_link_repoint both refused construction/archive/20260910-070937_itinerary-landed-accounts.md, whose block kept the card's own archive/ depth when a peer shelved it by hand. sh tools/fixtures/f/fold_shelf_link_repoint.sh rewrote the one link; both witnesses GREEN.
think Then the crux. Five ships met a full REDS pin in one morning and each asked Keaton for a bound raise. Rather than writing a sixth ask I ran sh tools/fixtures/r/reds_pin_capacity_scan.sh: pin_bytes=40771, bound 40960, 16 rows, all OPEN, pin_foldable_rows=0, pin_deadlocked=1, verdict=ok.
think %338 booked this deadlock on 20260829 and door B landed as the door that reaches the cause -- BOOKED split from OPEN, eight rows drained, the pin fell 24,828 to 5,388 bytes. Twelve days later it stands full again, so I read WHO holds each of the 16 rather than only whether each is open.
think Nine of the sixteen name Keaton, a custody gate, or a numbered gate; seven name Keaton's word outright. Door B split a live defect from a booked remainder and never split who can CLOSE a live one. Eight ships find reds at fleet rate and a row waiting on one person leaves at one person's rate, so the pin refills by mechanism rather than by a busy week.
think The second half is smaller. The over_bound_foldable cell has printed the exact command to type since %517; the deadlocked cell printed the diagnosis and stopped. That silence is what sent five careful hands to re-derive three doors already costed in an essay -- and one red, 20260910.064044, is cited in the card and in standing-equipment.kyri and in no ledger row at all.
obs The repair is reported and never gated. A gate over rows only one person may close would red hardest on the laps that found them, which is the reason %338's own capacity numbers report rather than refuse.
obs pin_held_rows is a PROXY over a row's own text, so the scan prints one detail: pin_held %N line per row and the header says so. A reader checks it; nobody trusts it.
obs My own row is born on a shelf, BOOKED, as %335 through %341 were -- and the shelf header says plainly that the birth is recorded practice rather than law, since %338's door C was costed and declined. Cited by stamp everywhere outside the ledger: shared_max reads 697 and local_max 698.
loom witness=standing_equipment_cold guards_run=235 guards_green=227 guards_red=6 guards_gated=2 guards_seconds=2590 tree_moved=no head_behind_anointed=0
